Subject: [PATCH] iOS sideload: Safari's file upload menu
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

content showed the system's document picker for every file input,
where Safari, and Chrome on WebKit, show a menu at the input: the photo
library, the camera or Files, depending on what the input accepts
(crbug.com/40255112). Hand file inputs to Chrome's file upload panel,
the one WKWebView's open panel uses. WebClient::RunFileChooser() takes
what content knows about the input: whether it takes several files, the
MIME types and extensions it accepts, whether it has a file already and
whether it asks for the camera. ChromeWebClient builds the
ChooseFileEvent the panel works from, and ChooseFileTabHelper places the
panel where the user tapped, as RunOpenPanel() does. The chosen files go
back to the page by path. Folders and saving keep the document picker.

Status: verified at Chromium 3313f827 in the iOS 27 simulator, with a
page that reports each input's files and reads the first one's bytes:
an input without accept shows 照片库, 拍摄照片或视频 and 选择文件 at the
input; image/* shows 拍摄照片 instead; .pdf goes straight to Files; a
photo from the library reached the page (IMG_0005.jpeg, all 1484524
bytes read, starting with a JPEG header); multiple took two photos;
tapping outside the menu or cancelling Files fired cancel. The camera
can't be checked in the simulator, where an input with capture shows
the menu. Not checked on a device.

